$NetBSD$

SysManage Server is installed, but it does NOT serve anything yet.

nginx is the front door and is REQUIRED, not optional.  The application
listens on loopback 127.0.0.1:8080 and serves the REST API and the agent
WebSocket only -- it has no static-file handler, so the web console is served
by nginx and by nothing else.  Until the steps below are done there is no
console to reach.

1. TLS certificate

   Install a certificate and key.  This package does not generate them: a
   certificate a package manufactured for you is one no client should trust.

     ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/sysmanage/tls/server.crt
     ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/sysmanage/tls/server.key

2. nginx configuration

   The shipped config is an EXAMPLE and is not read where it lands.  Copy it
   into place and include it:

     cp ${PREFIX}/share/examples/sysmanage/sysmanage-nginx.conf \
        ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/nginx/conf.d/sysmanage-nginx.conf
     # ensure ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/nginx/nginx.conf has, inside http { }:
     #     include ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/nginx/conf.d/*.conf;
     nginx -t
     /etc/rc.d/nginx start

   nginx will refuse to start until the certificate exists.  That is
   deliberate: a management console must not come up in cleartext because a
   file was missing.

3. Configuration file

     cp ${PREFIX}/share/examples/sysmanage/sysmanage.yaml \
        ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/sysmanage.yaml

   Then edit it -- at minimum the database connection.

4. Start the server

     /etc/rc.d/sysmanage start

   The console is then at https://<this-host>/ -- port 443 only.  Nothing
   needs to reach 8080 from outside this machine, and nothing should.

